/-!
# Composition of Koszul-regular, `H₁`-regular and quasi-regular immersions

The composite of two Koszul-regular immersions is Koszul-regular, the composite of two
`H₁`-regular immersions is `H₁`-regular, and the composite of an `H₁`-regular immersion followed
by a quasi-regular immersion is quasi-regular.  The three statements are proved first for
immersions of schemes, which is Stacks tag 067Q, and then for representable morphisms of
algebraic spaces over a scheme, which is Stacks tag 09S0.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isKoszulRegularImmersion_comp`,
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isH1RegularImmersion_comp` and
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isQuasiRegularImmersion_comp_of_isH1RegularImmersion`: **Stacks tag
  067Q**, parts (2), (3) and (4), for immersions of schemes.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isKoszulRegularImmersion_comp`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isH1RegularImmersion_comp` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasiRegularImmersion_comp_of_isH1RegularImmersion`: **Stacks tag
  09S0**, the same three statements for algebraic spaces.

## Implementation notes

The scheme-level argument is the affine-local one of the source, carried out in the
`AlgebraicGeometry.KerGeneratedBy` formulation of Stacks tag 063G: around a point of the image of
a closed immersion `j` an affine open `U` carries a family generating `RingHom.ker (j.app U)` with
the regularity property in question.  For a composite `i ≫ j` of closed immersions, shrink `U`
until `j ⁻¹ᵁ U` lies inside a witnessing affine open for `i`
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.exists_affineOpen_preimage_le_and_le`), restrict both families there
— restriction between affine opens is flat, so both regularity properties survive — and append to
the family for `j` a family of lifts along the surjection `j.app U` of the family for `i`.  The
kernel of `(i ≫ j).app U` is the contraction along `j.app U` of the kernel of `i.app (j ⁻¹ᵁ U)`,
which is exactly the ideal generated by the appended family, and the appended family is regular
by the concatenation theorems of Stacks tags 0669, 0668 and 0667.  That last step is the only
place the three cases differ, so it is abstracted into the hypotheses of `kerGeneratedBy_comp`,
which is stated for a pair of properties: the one asked of the outer immersion and carried by the
conclusion, and the one asked of the inner immersion.

The passage from closed immersions to immersions is the coborder bookkeeping already performed
for the regular case: `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.exists_open_isPullback_liftCoborder` produces an
open `W` of the target through which `i ≫ j` factors as a closed immersion, as the base change of
`j.liftCoborder` along an open immersion, and an open immersion is flat, so flat base change of
Stacks tag 067P restricts the regularity of `j` to `W`.

At the level of algebraic spaces both predicates are conditions on the base change of the
morphism to every étale scheme chart of the target, so the proof is: the base change of `i ≫ j`
to a chart `q` of `X` is, up to the comparison isomorphism of two cartesian squares, the
composite of the base change of `i` to the chart `hj.fst q` of `Y` and the base change of `j` to
`q`; the chart `hj.fst q` is étale because étaleness of a chart is stable under base change.  The
comparison isomorphism is absorbed by flat base change again, along the identity: precomposing an
immersion with an isomorphism is a base change of it along `𝟙`.

None of the three statements for algebraic spaces needs its source, intermediate object or
target to be an algebraic space, nor the two morphisms to be immersions in the sense of Stacks
tag 02YU: representability is part of each regularity predicate and the base changes to étale
charts are immersions of schemes by definition.  As with the predicates themselves in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Morphisms.PseudoCoherent.RegularImmersion`, algebraicity is
left to the caller.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.21.5 (Tag 067Q)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/067Q)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.21.4 (Tag 067P)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/067P)
* [Stacks Project, Definition 31.21.1 (Tag 063J)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063J)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 61.19.3 (Tag 09S0)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09S0)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

/-! ### Appending generators -/

section Algebra

/-- The ideal generated by a concatenation of two finite families is the sum of the ideals they
generate. -/
private theorem span_range_append {A : Type*} [CommRing A] {n m : ℕ} (f : Fin n → A)
    (g : Fin m → A) :
    Ideal.span (Set.range (Fin.append f g)) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range f) ⊔ Ideal.span (Set.range g) := by
  rw [← Ideal.span_union, ← Set.Sum.elim_range, ← Fin.append_comp_sumElim]
  exact congrArg Ideal.span (finSumFinEquiv.surjective.range_comp _).symm

/-- **The kernel of a composite of ring maps, generated by an appended family.**  Let `q` be
surjective with kernel generated by `f`, let the kernel of `r` be generated by `g`, and let `g'`
be a family of lifts of `g` along `q`.  Then the kernel of `r ∘ q` is generated by the
concatenation of `f` and `g'`. -/
private theorem ker_comp_eq_span_range_append {A B C : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [CommRing C] (q : A →+* B) (hq : Function.Surjective q) (r : B →+* C) {n m : ℕ}
    (f : Fin n → A) (g : Fin m → B) (g' : Fin m → A) (hg' : ∀ k, q (g' k) = g k)
    (hkerq : RingHom.ker q = Ideal.span (Set.range f))
    (hkerr : RingHom.ker r = Ideal.span (Set.range g)) :
    RingHom.ker (r.comp q) = Ideal.span (Set.range (Fin.append f g')) := by
  have hmap : Ideal.map q (Ideal.span (Set.range g')) = Ideal.span (Set.range g) := by
    rw [Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp, show ⇑q ∘ g' = g from funext hg']
  rw [span_range_append, ← RingHom.comap_ker r q, hkerr, ← hmap,
    Ideal.comap_map_of_surjective q hq, ← RingHom.ker_eq_comap_bot, hkerq]
  exact sup_comm _ _

/-- **A regularity property of the lifts, read in the quotient.**  Let `Q` be a property of finite
families of ring elements which survives a flat ring map.  If `q` is surjective with kernel
generated by `f` and the images of `g'` under `q` have `Q`, then so do the images of `g'` in the
quotient by the ideal generated by `f`: that quotient is isomorphic to the target of `q`, and an
isomorphism is in particular flat. -/
private theorem seq_quotient_of_surjective
    {Q : ∀ {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {r : ℕ}, (Fin r → A) → Prop}
    (hQflat : ∀ {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] (φ : A →+* B), φ.Flat →
      ∀ {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → A), Q f → Q fun i => φ (f i))
    {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    (q : A →+* B) (hq : Function.Surjective q) {n m : ℕ} (f : Fin n → A) (g' : Fin m → A)
    (hkerq : RingHom.ker q = Ideal.span (Set.range f)) (hg : Q fun k => q (g' k)) :
    Q fun k => Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span (Set.range f)) (g' k) := by
  let e : B ≃+* A ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f) :=
    (RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective hq).symm.trans (Ideal.quotEquivOfEq hkerq)
  have he : ∀ k, e (q (g' k)) = Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span (Set.range f)) (g' k) := by
    intro k
    show (Ideal.quotEquivOfEq hkerq)
      ((RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective hq).symm (q (g' k))) = _
    rw [RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective_symm_apply, Ideal.quotEquivOfEq_mk]
  have h := hQflat (e : B →+* A ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f))
    (RingHom.Flat.of_bijective e.bijective) (fun k => q (g' k)) hg
  simpa only [RingEquiv.coe_toRingHom, he] using h

end Algebra

/-! ### Composition of closed immersions -/

section ClosedComposition

/-- The restriction map between the rings of sections of two affine opens is flat. -/
private theorem flat_res {X : Scheme.{u}} {U V : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (hV : IsAffineOpen V) (hVU : V ≤ U) :
    (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVU).op).hom.Flat := by
  convert (𝟙 X : X ⟶ X).flat_appLE hU hV (by simpa using hVU) using 1
  show (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVU).op).hom =
    (CategoryStruct.id Γ(X, U) ≫ X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVU).op).hom
  rw [Category.id_comp]

/-- **Appending generators along a composite of closed immersions.**  Let `P` and `Q` be
properties of finite families of ring elements which survive a flat ring map, and suppose that a
family with `P` generating the kernel of a surjection stays `P` when concatenated with any family
whose image in the quotient has `Q`.  If the kernel of `i` is affine-locally generated by families
with `Q` and the kernel of `j` is affine-locally generated by families with `P`, then the kernel
of `i ≫ j` is affine-locally generated by families with `P`.

This is the whole affine-local content of Stacks tag 067Q for its three cases, which differ only
in the pair `(P, Q)`: Koszul-regular with Koszul-regular, `H₁`-regular with `H₁`-regular, and
quasi-regular with `H₁`-regular. -/
private theorem kerGeneratedBy_comp
    {P Q : ∀ {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {r : ℕ}, (Fin r → A) → Prop}
    (hflat : ∀ {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] (φ : A →+* B), φ.Flat →
      ∀ {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → A), P f → P fun i => φ (f i))
    (hQflat : ∀ {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] (φ : A →+* B), φ.Flat →
      ∀ {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → A), Q f → Q fun i => φ (f i))
    (happend : ∀ {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {n m : ℕ} (f : Fin n → A) (g : Fin m → A), P f →
      (Q fun k => Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span (Set.range f)) (g k)) → P (Fin.append f g))
    {Z Y X : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ Y) (j : Y ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion i] [IsClosedImmersion j]
    (hi : KerGeneratedBy Q i) (hj : KerGeneratedBy P j) :
    KerGeneratedBy P (i ≫ j) := by
  classical
  intro x hx
  rw [(IsClosedImmersion.isClosedEmbedding (i ≫ j)).isClosed_range.closure_eq] at hx
  obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := hx
  have hxj : j (i z) = (i ≫ j) z := (Scheme.Hom.comp_apply i j z).symm
  obtain ⟨U₀, hzU₀, n, f₀, hkerf₀, hf₀⟩ := hj (j (i z)) (subset_closure ⟨i z, rfl⟩)
  obtain ⟨V₀, hzV₀, m, g₀, hkerg₀, hg₀⟩ := hi (i z) (subset_closure ⟨z, rfl⟩)
  obtain ⟨U, hzU, hUV, hUU₀⟩ :=
    exists_affineOpen_preimage_le_and_le j V₀.1 U₀.1 hzV₀ hzU₀
  have hV : IsAffineOpen (j ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) := U.2.preimage j
  -- the two generating families, restricted to `U` and to `j ⁻¹ᵁ U`
  have hkerf : RingHom.ker (j.app U.1).hom =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun k => (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hUU₀).op).hom (f₀ k)) := by
    rw [ker_app_eq_map_ker_app j U₀.2 U.2 hUU₀, hkerf₀, Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
    rfl
  have hkerg : RingHom.ker (i.app (j ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)).hom =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun k => (Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE hUV).op).hom (g₀ k)) := by
    rw [ker_app_eq_map_ker_app i V₀.2 hV hUV, hkerg₀, Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
    rfl
  have hf : P fun k => (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hUU₀).op).hom (f₀ k) :=
    hflat _ (flat_res U₀.2 U.2 hUU₀) f₀ hf₀
  have hg : Q fun k => (Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE hUV).op).hom (g₀ k) :=
    hQflat _ (flat_res V₀.2 hV hUV) g₀ hg₀
  -- lift the inner family along the surjection `j.app U`
  have hq : Function.Surjective (j.app U.1).hom := j.app_surjective U.1 U.2
  choose g' hg' using fun k => hq ((Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE hUV).op).hom (g₀ k))
  have hcomp : ((i ≫ j).app U.1).hom = (i.app (j ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)).hom.comp (j.app U.1).hom :=
    (congrArg CommRingCat.Hom.hom (Scheme.Hom.comp_app i j U.1)).trans (CommRingCat.hom_comp _ _)
  refine ⟨U, hxj ▸ hzU, n + m,
    Fin.append (fun k => (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hUU₀).op).hom (f₀ k)) g', ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [hcomp]
    exact ker_comp_eq_span_range_append _ hq _ _ _ g' hg' hkerf hkerg
  · refine happend _ g' hf (seq_quotient_of_surjective hQflat _ hq _ g' hkerf ?_)
    simpa only [hg'] using hg

/-- **Stacks tag 067Q, the Koszul-regular case for closed immersions.**  The composite of two
closed immersions with Koszul-regular defining ideal sheaves has a Koszul-regular defining ideal
sheaf. -/
theorem isKoszulRegularIdealSheaf_comp_of_isClosedImmersion {Z Y X : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ Y)
    (j : Y ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion i] [IsClosedImmersion j]
    (hi : IsKoszulRegularIdealSheaf Y.toRingedSpace (definingIdealOfHom i))
    (hj : IsKoszulRegularIdealSheaf X.toRingedSpace (definingIdealOfHom j)) :
    IsKoszulRegularIdealSheaf X.toRingedSpace (definingIdealOfHom (i ≫ j)) :=
  (isKoszulRegularIdealSheaf_iff_kerGeneratedBy (i ≫ j)).mpr
    (kerGeneratedBy_comp isKoszulRegular_of_ringHomFlat isKoszulRegular_of_ringHomFlat
      (fun f g hf hg => Koszul.koszul_regular_append f g hf hg) i j
      ((isKoszulRegularIdealSheaf_iff_kerGeneratedBy i).mp hi)
      ((isKoszulRegularIdealSheaf_iff_kerGeneratedBy j).mp hj))

/-- **Stacks tag 067Q, the `H₁`-regular case for closed immersions.**  The composite of two closed
immersions with `H₁`-regular defining ideal sheaves has an `H₁`-regular defining ideal sheaf. -/
theorem isH1RegularIdealSheaf_comp_of_isClosedImmersion {Z Y X : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ Y)
    (j : Y ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion i] [IsClosedImmersion j]
    (hi : IsH1RegularIdealSheaf Y.toRingedSpace (definingIdealOfHom i))
    (hj : IsH1RegularIdealSheaf X.toRingedSpace (definingIdealOfHom j)) :
    IsH1RegularIdealSheaf X.toRingedSpace (definingIdealOfHom (i ≫ j)) :=
  (isH1RegularIdealSheaf_iff_kerGeneratedBy (i ≫ j)).mpr
    (kerGeneratedBy_comp isH1Regular_of_ringHomFlat isH1Regular_of_ringHomFlat
      (fun f g hf hg => Koszul.isH1Regular_append f g hf hg) i j
      ((isH1RegularIdealSheaf_iff_kerGeneratedBy i).mp hi)
      ((isH1RegularIdealSheaf_iff_kerGeneratedBy j).mp hj))

/-- **Stacks tag 067Q, the mixed case for closed immersions.**  The composite of a closed
immersion with an `H₁`-regular defining ideal sheaf and a closed immersion with a quasi-regular
defining ideal sheaf has a quasi-regular defining ideal sheaf. -/
theorem isQuasiRegularIdealSheaf_comp_of_isClosedImmersion {Z Y X : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ Y)
    (j : Y ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion i] [IsClosedImmersion j]
    (hi : IsH1RegularIdealSheaf Y.toRingedSpace (definingIdealOfHom i))
    (hj : IsQuasiRegularIdealSheaf X.toRingedSpace (definingIdealOfHom j)) :
    IsQuasiRegularIdealSheaf X.toRingedSpace (definingIdealOfHom (i ≫ j)) :=
  (isQuasiRegularIdealSheaf_iff_kerGeneratedBy (i ≫ j)).mpr
    (kerGeneratedBy_comp isQuasiRegular_of_ringHomFlat isH1Regular_of_ringHomFlat
      (fun f g hf hg => Koszul.isQuasiRegular_append_of_isH1Regular_quotient f g hf hg) i j
      ((isH1RegularIdealSheaf_iff_kerGeneratedBy i).mp hi)
      ((isQuasiRegularIdealSheaf_iff_kerGeneratedBy j).mp hj))

end ClosedComposition

/-! ### Composition of immersions of schemes -/

section Composition

/-- **Stacks tag 067Q, the Koszul-regular case.**  The composite of two Koszul-regular immersions
of schemes is a Koszul-regular immersion. -/
@[stacks 067Q "composition_koszul_regular", sga "6 VII 1.7", sga "6 VIII 1.1", sga "6 VIII 1.3"]
theorem isKoszulRegularImmersion_comp {Z Y X : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ Y) (j : Y ⟶ X)
    [IsImmersion i] [IsImmersion j] (hi : IsKoszulRegularImmersion i)
    (hj : IsKoszulRegularImmersion j) :
    IsKoszulRegularImmersion (i ≫ j) := by
  obtain ⟨W, b, j', _, H, hj'⟩ := exists_open_isPullback_liftCoborder j i.coborderRange
  have : IsClosedImmersion j' := MorphismProperty.of_isPullback H.flip inferInstance
  have hjreg : IsKoszulRegularIdealSheaf W.toScheme.toRingedSpace (definingIdealOfHom j') :=
    isKoszulRegularIdealSheaf_definingIdealOfHom_of_isPullback_of_flat H
      ((isKoszulRegularImmersion_iff_of_open j j.coborderRange j.liftCoborder
        j.liftCoborder_ι).mp hj)
  have hcomp := isKoszulRegularIdealSheaf_comp_of_isClosedImmersion i.liftCoborder j'
    ((isKoszulRegularImmersion_iff_of_open i i.coborderRange i.liftCoborder
      i.liftCoborder_ι).mp hi) hjreg
  refine (isKoszulRegularImmersion_iff_of_open (i ≫ j) W (i.liftCoborder ≫ j') ?_).mpr hcomp
  rw [Category.assoc, hj', ← Category.assoc, i.liftCoborder_ι]

/-- **Stacks tag 067Q, the `H₁`-regular case.**  The composite of two `H₁`-regular immersions of
schemes is an `H₁`-regular immersion. -/
@[stacks 067Q "composition_h1_regular"]
theorem isH1RegularImmersion_comp {Z Y X : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ Y) (j : Y ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i]
    [IsImmersion j] (hi : IsH1RegularImmersion i) (hj : IsH1RegularImmersion j) :
    IsH1RegularImmersion (i ≫ j) := by
  obtain ⟨W, b, j', _, H, hj'⟩ := exists_open_isPullback_liftCoborder j i.coborderRange
  have : IsClosedImmersion j' := MorphismProperty.of_isPullback H.flip inferInstance
  have hjreg : IsH1RegularIdealSheaf W.toScheme.toRingedSpace (definingIdealOfHom j') :=
    isH1RegularIdealSheaf_definingIdealOfHom_of_isPullback_of_flat H
      ((isH1RegularImmersion_iff_of_open j j.coborderRange j.liftCoborder
        j.liftCoborder_ι).mp hj)
  have hcomp := isH1RegularIdealSheaf_comp_of_isClosedImmersion i.liftCoborder j'
    ((isH1RegularImmersion_iff_of_open i i.coborderRange i.liftCoborder
      i.liftCoborder_ι).mp hi) hjreg
  refine (isH1RegularImmersion_iff_of_open (i ≫ j) W (i.liftCoborder ≫ j') ?_).mpr hcomp
  rw [Category.assoc, hj', ← Category.assoc, i.liftCoborder_ι]

/-- **Stacks tag 067Q, the mixed case.**  The composite of an `H₁`-regular immersion of schemes
and a quasi-regular immersion of schemes is a quasi-regular immersion. -/
@[stacks 067Q "composition_h1_quasi_regular"]
theorem isQuasiRegularImmersion_comp_of_isH1RegularImmersion {Z Y X : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ Y)
    (j : Y ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i] [IsImmersion j] (hi : IsH1RegularImmersion i)
    (hj : IsQuasiRegularImmersion j) :
    IsQuasiRegularImmersion (i ≫ j) := by
  obtain ⟨W, b, j', _, H, hj'⟩ := exists_open_isPullback_liftCoborder j i.coborderRange
  have : IsClosedImmersion j' := MorphismProperty.of_isPullback H.flip inferInstance
  have hjreg : IsQuasiRegularIdealSheaf W.toScheme.toRingedSpace (definingIdealOfHom j') :=
    isQuasiRegularIdealSheaf_definingIdealOfHom_of_isPullback_of_flat H
      ((isQuasiRegularImmersion_iff_of_open j j.coborderRange j.liftCoborder
        j.liftCoborder_ι).mp hj)
  have hcomp := isQuasiRegularIdealSheaf_comp_of_isClosedImmersion i.liftCoborder j'
    ((isH1RegularImmersion_iff_of_open i i.coborderRange i.liftCoborder
      i.liftCoborder_ι).mp hi) hjreg
  refine (isQuasiRegularImmersion_iff_of_open (i ≫ j) W (i.liftCoborder ≫ j') ?_).mpr hcomp
  rw [Category.assoc, hj', ← Category.assoc, i.liftCoborder_ι]

/-- Precomposing a Koszul-regular immersion with an isomorphism gives a Koszul-regular immersion:
the resulting square over the identity is cartesian, and the identity is flat. -/
theorem isKoszulRegularImmersion_iso_hom_comp {A B X : Scheme.{u}} (e : A ≅ B) (f : B ⟶ X)
    [IsImmersion f] (hf : IsKoszulRegularImmersion f) : IsKoszulRegularImmersion (e.hom ≫ f) :=
  isKoszulRegularImmersion_of_isPullback_of_flat
    (IsPullback.of_vert_isIso ⟨by rw [Category.comp_id]⟩) hf

/-- Precomposing an `H₁`-regular immersion with an isomorphism gives an `H₁`-regular immersion. -/
theorem isH1RegularImmersion_iso_hom_comp {A B X : Scheme.{u}} (e : A ≅ B) (f : B ⟶ X)
    [IsImmersion f] (hf : IsH1RegularImmersion f) : IsH1RegularImmersion (e.hom ≫ f) :=
  isH1RegularImmersion_of_isPullback_of_flat
    (IsPullback.of_vert_isIso ⟨by rw [Category.comp_id]⟩) hf

/-- Precomposing a quasi-regular immersion with an isomorphism gives a quasi-regular
immersion. -/
theorem isQuasiRegularImmersion_iso_hom_comp {A B X : Scheme.{u}} (e : A ≅ B) (f : B ⟶ X)
    [IsImmersion f] (hf : IsQuasiRegularImmersion f) : IsQuasiRegularImmersion (e.hom ≫ f) :=
  isQuasiRegularImmersion_of_isPullback_of_flat
    (IsPullback.of_vert_isIso ⟨by rw [Category.comp_id]⟩) hf

end Composition

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry

/-! ### Composition of immersions of algebraic spaces -/

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

universe u

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    {Z Y X : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u}

/-- **The base change of a composite to a chart is the composite of the base changes.**  For a
chart `q` of `X` the canonical represented base change of `i ≫ j` along `q` is isomorphic, over
the two factors, to the base change of `i` along the chart `hj.fst q` of `Y` followed by the base
change of `j` along `q`. -/
private theorem exists_comparisonIso_of_comp {i : Z ⟶ Y} {j : Y ⟶ X}
    (hi : yoneda.relativelyRepresentable i) (hj : yoneda.relativelyRepresentable j)
    (hij : yoneda.relativelyRepresentable (i ≫ j)) {V : BigFppfOver B S hS}
    (q : yoneda.obj V ⟶ X) :
    ∃ e : (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (hij.pullback q) ≅
        (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (hi.pullback (hj.fst q)),
      e.hom ≫ ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (hi.snd (hj.fst q)) ≫
          (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (hj.snd q)) =
        (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (hij.snd q) := by
  have hOuter : IsPullback (hi.fst (hj.fst q))
      (yoneda.map (hi.snd (hj.fst q) ≫ hj.snd q)) (i ≫ j) q := by
    simpa only [Functor.map_comp] using
      ((hi.isPullback (hj.fst q)).flip.paste_horiz (hj.isPullback q).flip).flip
  have hPB := hij.isPullback q
  refine ⟨(BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).mapIso
    (yoneda.preimageIso (hPB.isoIsPullback _ _ hOuter)), ?_⟩
  have he : (yoneda.preimageIso (hPB.isoIsPullback _ _ hOuter)).hom ≫
      (hi.snd (hj.fst q) ≫ hj.snd q) = hij.snd q := by
    apply yoneda.map_injective
    rw [Functor.map_comp]
    simpa only [Functor.preimageIso_hom, Functor.map_preimage] using
      hPB.isoIsPullback_hom_snd _ _ hOuter
  simpa only [Functor.mapIso_hom, Functor.map_comp] using
    congrArg (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map he

/-- A representable morphism of algebraic spaces over `S` whose base change to every étale scheme
chart of the target is an immersion of schemes with the property `P`. -/
private abbrev ChartwiseImmersion
    (P : ∀ {A C : Scheme.{u}} (f : A ⟶ C) [_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.IsImmersion f], Prop)
    (i : Z ⟶ Y) : Prop :=
  ∃ hi : yoneda.relativelyRepresentable i,
    ∀ (V : BigFppfOver B S hS) (q : yoneda.obj V ⟶ Y),
      (MorphismProperty.inverseImage (@Etale.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
        (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf q →
      ∃ hj : _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.IsImmersion ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (hi.snd q)),
        @P _ _ ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (hi.snd q)) hj

/-- **Composition for algebraic spaces from composition for schemes.**  If `Pi` and `Pj` compose
to `Pc` for immersions of schemes, and `Pc` is stable under precomposition with an isomorphism,
then the composite of a `Pi`-chartwise and a `Pj`-chartwise immersion is `Pc`-chartwise. -/
private theorem chartwiseImmersion_comp
    {Pi Pj Pc : ∀ {A C : Scheme.{u}} (f : A ⟶ C) [_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.IsImmersion f], Prop}
    (hcomp : ∀ {A C D : Scheme.{u}} (f : A ⟶ C) (g : C ⟶ D)
      [_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.IsImmersion f] [_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.IsImmersion g],
      Pi f → Pj g → Pc (f ≫ g))
    (hiso : ∀ {A C D : Scheme.{u}} (e : A ≅ C) (f : C ⟶ D)
      [_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.IsImmersion f], Pc f → Pc (e.hom ≫ f))
    {i : Z ⟶ Y} {j : Y ⟶ X} (hi : ChartwiseImmersion B S hS Pi i)
    (hj : ChartwiseImmersion B S hS Pj j) : ChartwiseImmersion B S hS Pc (i ≫ j) := by
  obtain ⟨hri, hiall⟩ := hi
  obtain ⟨hrj, hjall⟩ := hj
  refine ⟨MorphismProperty.comp_mem _ i j hri hrj, fun V q hq => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨hImmOut, hOut⟩ := hjall V q hq
  obtain ⟨hImmIn, hIn⟩ := hiall (hrj.pullback q) (hrj.fst q)
    (presheaf_of_isPullback B S hS (hrj.isPullback q).flip hq)
  obtain ⟨e, heSch⟩ := exists_comparisonIso_of_comp B S hS hri hrj _ q
  rw [← heSch]
  exact ⟨inferInstance, hiso e _ (hcomp _ _ hIn hOut)⟩

/-- **Stacks 09S0, the Koszul-regular case.**  The composite of two Koszul-regular immersions of
algebraic spaces over `S` is a Koszul-regular immersion. -/
@[stacks 09S0 "composition of Koszul-regular immersions"]
theorem isKoszulRegularImmersion_comp (i : Z ⟶ Y) (j : Y ⟶ X)
    (hi : IsKoszulRegularImmersion B S hS i) (hj : IsKoszulRegularImmersion B S hS j) :
    IsKoszulRegularImmersion B S hS (i ≫ j) :=
  chartwiseImmersion_comp B S hS Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isKoszulRegularImmersion_comp
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isKoszulRegularImmersion_iso_hom_comp hi hj

/-- **Stacks 09S0, the `H₁`-regular case.**  The composite of two `H₁`-regular immersions of
algebraic spaces over `S` is an `H₁`-regular immersion. -/
@[stacks 09S0 "composition of H₁-regular immersions"]
theorem isH1RegularImmersion_comp (i : Z ⟶ Y) (j : Y ⟶ X)
    (hi : IsH1RegularImmersion B S hS i) (hj : IsH1RegularImmersion B S hS j) :
    IsH1RegularImmersion B S hS (i ≫ j) :=
  chartwiseImmersion_comp B S hS Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isH1RegularImmersion_comp
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isH1RegularImmersion_iso_hom_comp hi hj

/-- **Stacks 09S0, the mixed case.**  The composite of an `H₁`-regular immersion of algebraic
spaces over `S` and a quasi-regular immersion of algebraic spaces over `S` is a quasi-regular
immersion. -/
@[stacks 09S0 "composition of an H₁-regular and a quasi-regular immersion"]
theorem isQuasiRegularImmersion_comp_of_isH1RegularImmersion (i : Z ⟶ Y) (j : Y ⟶ X)
    (hi : IsH1RegularImmersion B S hS i) (hj : IsQuasiRegularImmersion B S hS j) :
    IsQuasiRegularImmersion B S hS (i ≫ j) :=
  chartwiseImmersion_comp B S hS
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isQuasiRegularImmersion_comp_of_isH1RegularImmersion
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isQuasiRegularImmersion_iso_hom_comp hi hj

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

